.TH "RAPTOR-SET" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-set \- Apply each PATH=VALUE to MODEL and save. Writes to \-o OUT, or with \-\-in\-place to MODEL itself (a .bak copy is kept with \-\-backup). Without either, nothing is written.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor set\fR [\-h] [\-\-set\-file FILE] [\-o OUT | \-\-in\-place] [\-\-backup] MODEL [PATH=VALUE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply each PATH=VALUE to MODEL and save. Writes to \-o OUT, or with \-\-in\-place to MODEL itself (a .bak copy is kept with \-\-backup). Without either, nothing is written.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fIFILE\fR

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIOUT\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-backup\fR
with \-\-in\-place, keep MODEL.bak
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Change a setting and save under a new name.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor set pump.rbd system.runs=200 \-o pump200.rbds\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Change in place, keeping pump.rbds.bak.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor set pump.rbds system.runs=200 \-\-in\-place \-\-backup\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1), \fBraptor\-set\-paths\fR(7)
